# What the pins in sources.lock are for: build/pins-table.sh joins this file
# with sources.lock into the overview tables of the README and the release
# notes. Versions and commits come from sources.lock only, never from here.
#
#   product <id> | <name> | <sources> | <how it is tested>
#   change  <source> | <base> | <what it changes or fixes> | <how the change is tested> | <upstream>
#
# A "change" line is for every pin that is not a plain upstream release: a
# fork commit or a development commit. Fields are Markdown, one line each.
# <upstream>: the pull requests and issues (owner/repo#N, space-separated)
# that carry the change upstream; check-upstream.sh reports their state, and
# once all are merged or fixed the pin can go back to an upstream release.

product linux        | Linux client `sdl-freerdp` + `freerdp-tk` | freerdp sdl3 sdl3_ttf freetype openssl opus dav1d avm zlib jansson freerdp_tk python_linux_x86_64 python_linux_aarch64 | `build/check-portable.sh` (only glibc ≥ 2.34, libgcc_s and libpulse from the host), `test/smoke.sh` (starts and finds its libraries on Alma 9, Rocky 10, Debian 12/13, Ubuntu 22.04/24.04, Fedora 43, Tumbleweed, Arch; there the bundled Python loads Tk and freerdp-tk)
product windows      | Windows client `sdl-freerdp.exe` + `freerdp-tk` | freerdp sdl3 sdl3_ttf freetype libressl opus dav1d avm zlib jansson llvm_mingw freerdp_tk python_windows_x86_64 python_windows_aarch64 | `build/check-windows.sh` (needs only Windows' own DLLs)
product macos        | macOS client `sdl-freerdp` + `freerdp-tk` | freerdp sdl3 sdl3_ttf freetype openssl opus dav1d avm zlib jansson freerdp_tk python_macos_arm64 python_macos_x86_64 | `build/check-macos.sh` (only macOS's own libraries and frameworks, minimum macOS 12.0, an ad-hoc signature); the bundled Python loads Tk and freerdp-tk; arm64 on macos-15, x86_64 on macos-15-intel
product windows_host | Windows host `freerdp-shadow-service` + `freerdp-shadow-cli` | freerdp_host libressl opus dav1d aom avm zlib jansson llvm_mingw | `build/check-windows.sh`, then `test/windows-host.ps1` on a Windows Server 2025 runner: the service runs the server as SYSTEM on the console session, Windows-account logins, AV1, Ctrl+Alt+Del and the lock screen followed, a Unix socket; and the web client logs in through websockify
product web          | Web client + freerdp-web page | freerdp sdl3_wasm sdl3_ttf freetype libressl opus dav1d avm zlib jansson freerdp_web | `test/wasm-session.sh`: a browser logs in to xrdp through SSH + websockify, the page served without COOP/COEP headers (as GitHub Pages)
product xrdp         | xrdp packages (.deb, .rpm) | xrdp librfxcodec libpainter xorgxrdp x264 opus pipewire_xrdp mutter | `check-deps.sh`, then `test/xrdp-session.sh`: install in a fresh container of each release, log in over RDP: an Xorg session (xorgxrdp) with an xterm, then a Wayland one (sway, unless the release is marked no-sway) captured at the client's size; the login screen lists GNOME, and KDE unless no-kde; the default is GNOME on Fedora (Wayland first), Xorg elsewhere
product mac_host     | macOS host `FreeRDP-Shadow.app`  | freerdp_mac_host openssl opus dav1d aom avm zlib jansson | `.github/workflows/mac-host.yml` builds and packages it on both architectures; the capture is tested by hand on a Mac (CI cannot grant Screen Recording)

change freerdp          | FreeRDP master @ dae0390a4 (2026-10-31) | our release-20261031.9, picked from integration-latest on the fork: every client, native and web, builds it, not an upstream release. Master already carries our merged AV1 #13731, sound #13732, H.264 through WebCodecs #13812, #13838, #13839, the Web Audio microphone #13811, the Emscripten clipboard #13733, MessageChannel yield #13864 and monitors #13865, no connection dialog window #13860, SDL3 clipboard events #13872 and hotkeys from the key event's own modifiers #13852. On top, 10 commits of open pull requests: the AV2 extension (#13925: the clients decode AV2 with libavm and offer it; the web client with a decoder-only libavm), the physical monitor size in millimetres (#13805: SDL3 sent pixels, so a 2880-pixel window was a 2.88 m monitor), xrdp's padded legacy bitmaps accepted again (#13946: master 343f23134, #13884, dropped the session), the SDL3 dialog and clipboard queues no longer reading a freed item (#13961: master d5d230ddd's `auto&` on a popped item garbled the connection messages), and a wave that does not decode dropped while sound plays on (#13957). TLS 1.3 to Windows Server 2025's own Remote Desktop: the cause is LibreSSL's ClientHello (libressl/portable#1452), fixed by the kit's LibreSSL patch; the earlier TLS 1.2 retry (#13944, closed) is gone | the native clients' smoke and xrdp login tests (with /bpp:24 typing: legacy bitmaps), the web login test, the Windows test (the browser and freerdp-tk to Windows' own Remote Desktop); before the pick: ctest 211/211, kit test round 41199723802 (every FreeRDP check), freerdp-59's xrdp sway e2e 57/57 | FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13805 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13925 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13946 libressl/portable#1452 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13957 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13961
change freerdp_host     | FreeRDP master @ 472f1901f (2026-10-30) | our release-20261030.2, picked from integration-shadow-win: the Windows shadow server's two build fixes, DXGI capture that follows the secure desktop, freerdp-shadow-service with Ctrl+Alt+Del, a Unix-socket listener on Windows, a refresh request answered with the whole screen, AV2 (FreeRDP#13925: libavm encodes, `/gfx-av2`), the sound the PC plays (WASAPI loopback; its rdpsnd fixes #13943), the screen's true size (a 1600 x 900 screen was 1601 x 901); uninstall puts back the Ctrl+Alt+Del policy as install found it; the keys a client leaves held are let go when it leaves or sends a Synchronize (#13958) | `test/windows-host.ps1` (Windows Server 2025 runner) | FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13931 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13932 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13933 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13934 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13935 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13943 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13954 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13956 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13958
change avm              | AVM (AV2 reference) main, our fork | its release {version} on congzhangzh/avm: libavm, AV2's reference encoder and decoder, with our realtime speed work (cpu-used 9 for screens, 10 for camera-like content, tiles packed on the encoder's threads); built with the two ML encoder experiments off (no TensorFlow Lite), as its release kit does | its release kit's gate (56/56 decode vectors on x86_64, aarch64, wasm), then here the AV2 session on the Windows host (`test/windows-host.ps1`) | —
change sdl3_wasm        | SDL `release-3.4.18` | 1 commit: the Emscripten timers are safe to use from any thread. Since 4d8f84f161 (in 3.2.30 and 3.4) they run with pthreads too, but a timeout belongs to the thread that set it: a timer removed from another thread fired through a freed entry ("table index is out of bounds" in `SDL_Emscripten_TimerHelper`), in about 1 of 3 first sessions. 3.4.18 already has upstream's `FS.mkdir("/tmp/filedrop")` guard, which 3.2.30 needed backported (a second window, FreeRDP's retry dialog, threw `EEXIST` and hung a JSPI client after a network drop) | freerdp-web's whole suite on Asyncify and JSPI builds, 28 of 28 runs, `test-capture` and `test-reconnect` included, with the page's pointer-event fix (SDL 3.4 reads the mouse from pointer events); `SDL_timer.c` compiles with `-Werror` | libsdl-org/SDL#16587
change freerdp_tk       | its release {version} | our own connection window (Tkinter), shipped with the clients and their Python; `freerdp-tk` / `freerdp-tk.cmd` starts it. Since 0.3.0 it keeps passwords in the system's own store (Credential Manager, Keychain, Secret Service or KWallet) through keyring: the kit bundles keyring and what it needs on each OS, at the versions and SHA-256 of freerdp-tk's own uv.lock (`build/launcher.sh`, add_tk_deps) | the smoke test loads it with the bundled Python on every distribution; the build imports keyring and its backend's libraries with it (Linux, macOS)
change freerdp_web      | its release {version} | our own page, taken by its release tag | its unit tests and page checks (freerdp-web CI), then the web login test
change xrdp             | xrdp devel @ 5943357a (2026-10-14) | 128 commits on their way upstream: AV2 with libavm (avm-6e's encoder, FreeRDP's FRDP_2 / AV2 codec id; built with --enable-av2, off in the codec order until the server puts it first), Wayland sessions (wlup: sway, GNOME, KDE), GNOME and KDE with a monitor per RDP monitor and the client's primary as their own (branches feature-wlup-mutter-multimon, feature-wlup-kwin-multimon), and a max_fps setting for them, KWin 6.8's custom modes (kde_output_management_v2 22), AV1 with 4:4:4, encoder paced by the client's frame acknowledgements, Opus sound fixes (#3922: 2 of its 3 commits); plus the JPEG quality byte compared as unsigned, so it builds on ARM64 (branch caps-jpeg-quality-unsigned) | the login test, Xorg and Wayland, on x86_64 and ARM64; the ARM64 fix also by a build with -funsigned-char, which fails without it | neutrinolabs/xrdp#3904 neutrinolabs/xrdp#3911 neutrinolabs/xrdp#3912 neutrinolabs/xrdp#3913 neutrinolabs/xrdp#3914 neutrinolabs/xrdp#3915 neutrinolabs/xrdp#3922
change librfxcodec      | xrdp's submodule | unchanged: the commit `xrdp` uses | built with xrdp
change libpainter       | xrdp's submodule | unchanged: the commit `xrdp` uses | built with xrdp
change xorgxrdp         | xorgxrdp devel | unchanged: the development commit whose module interface `xrdp` needs | the Xorg login
change x264             | x264 `stable` branch | unchanged: x264 has no releases | the xrdp login tests (H.264)
change pipewire_xrdp    | release v{version} | unchanged, pinned by its tag's commit; built for Fedora only, which does not package it | built in the Fedora xrdp jobs
change mutter           | Fedora 45's {version} | an opt-in for Fedora 45: Fedora's own source package plus our fix for a Wayland window that lands on the wrong monitor when the monitor layout moves its monitor (2 commits, patches/mutter/: the main monitor from the newest pending move after a layout change, also when the client acks an older configure; as of 2026-10-28), release 1.0kit1, so Fedora's next update replaces it | 20 of 20 runs of the All screens check on the right monitor (stock 51.0: 1 of 10 wrong; 0 of 11 vs 5 of 7 with the server on one CPU); build/build-mutter.sh installs it with Fedora's gnome-shell | GNOME/mutter#5162 GNOME/mutter!5438
change freerdp_mac_host  | FreeRDP master @ dae0390a4 (2026-10-31) | our release-20261031.10, picked from integration-shadow-mac (freerdp-d0's): the shadow server built on macOS again, ScreenCaptureKit capture of every display with the sound the Mac plays, Quartz input, the cursor drawn by the client, capture again after the display sleeps; logins are the Mac's own (PAM, /sec:tls); with the AV2 extension and the shadow server's rdpsnd fixes; since release-20261031.10 the extended keys (both Command keys, arrows, Home/End, PgUp/PgDn, Forward Delete, keypad Enter, right Option) reach the Mac | a compile and package on GitHub's macOS runners (both architectures); 聪哥's live session on his Mac (login, cursor, Opus sound, input) | FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13925 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13943 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13948 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13952 FreeRDP/FreeRDP#13953
